  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt against TestFramework.Azure 0.3.0 and TestFramework.Core 0.3.0. No API change in this package.\nInherited BREAKING change: teardown now deletes an artifact a run discovered unless the declaring step chains MarkReadonly(). For Azure that means a SQL row located by the EF Core finder, which was previously never deleted; Cosmos items and Table entities already behaved this way.\nIn container mode this is usually invisible: the emulator the run started is discarded when the environment tears down, so deleting a row inside it changes nothing observable. It matters the moment the same timeline is pointed at a store that outlives the run - a shared emulator, a persistent environment, or live Azure. Add MarkReadonly() to discovery steps before doing that.",
